'''Tuanul''' was a settlement on the [[planet]] [[Jakku]]<ref name="Aftermath" /> located in [[Kelvin Ravine]]. It was populated by members of the [[Church of the Force]],<ref name="Visual" /> who eschewed modern technology and instead created their own in order to bring themselves more in touch with nature.<ref name="Empire's End">''[[Aftermath: Empire's End]]''</ref>

==Description==
The huts of Tuanul were made of wattle and daub created from local natural materials.<ref name="VE">''[[Star Wars: The Visual Encyclopedia]]''</ref>

==History==
[[File:Tuanul-TFA.png|thumb|left|250px|The village shortly before the First Order's attack in 34 ABY]]
[[34 ABY|Thirty]] [[Standard year|years]] after the [[Battle of Endor]],<ref name="Date">''[[Star Wars: Galactic Atlas]]'' places the events of the film [[Star Wars: Episode VII The Force Awakens|''Star Wars'': Episode VII ''The Force Awakens'']] in [[34 ABY]]</ref> during a [[Cold War|conflict]] between the [[First Order]] and the [[Resistance]], the settlement was [[Attack on Tuanul|sacked]] by the Order. The assault was led by [[Ben Solo|Kylo Ren]], a [[Force-sensitive|Force]] [[Soldier|warrior]] who sought to gain [[Map to Skywalker|knowledge]] on the whereabouts of the missing [[Jedi Master]] [[Luke Skywalker]] from one of the Tuanul villagers, [[Lor San Tekka]]. After capturing the [[Resistance pilot]] [[Poe Dameron]], the [[First Order stormtrooper|stormtroopers]]&mdash;with the exception of [[Finn|FN-2187]]&mdash;[[Death|executed]] the villagers in accordance with Ren's orders.<ref name="Episode VII">{{Film|VII}}</ref>

